  b: single-scalar-status
split: leaning
draft_status: axis-only
leverage: 13.4
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(16) x split_weight(0.7) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.2)"

question: >
  On status dimensionality — whether a record's standing is reported as several
  orthogonal axes, or collapsed into one value — the records assert both multi
  axis status (12 judgments, 8 authored) and single scalar status (4 judgments,
  0 authored). Which should be the stated rule, and where is the exception?

why_it_matters: >
  Until this is answered, a record below Dave inherits whichever side it happens
  to copy. Full draft pending: the proposal batch for this axis did not
  complete; the axis, poles, counts and evidence are real, the options below are
  the generic form.

